Z||000000||RiceCooker||04-12-2001||05:03 PM||||Has anyone ever had problems with UPS not picking something up?<P>Has anyone had any problems with Fiershop in CA?<P>I ordered my clutch release lever from Fieroshop on MONDAY. I was happy because i was getting a new part and i might be able to have my daily driver and only car back on the road within a couple days. I was under the impression that the part would be picked up that afternoon and shipped overnight - maybe taking two days beacuse of customs etc etc.<P>Well I'm checking the tracking # and not getting anything because the part is still at Fieroshop!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Just wondering if UPS does this quite often because i could have got this part off of someone else on Tuesday and shipped here by now.<P>Sorry for the long post, thanks for the help<BR>Todd  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Kids in the back seat cause accidents<BR>Accidents in the back seat cause kids||||reg||5
Z||000001||JSocha||04-12-2001||05:11 PM||||I've recently ordered a few things now from them and they were here a few days later (3 working days).<P>Did they have the part in stock when you ordered???  That maybe the reason its late now.<P>just a brain fart here...||||reg||1
Z||000002||stsmithgt||04-12-2001||05:46 PM||||They <I>do</I> have phone numbers.  Ones that I should use.  Talk to George or Terry.  I don't believe they'd be yanking your chain.  I need to get my car back there, but I keep putting off calling because we're so busy at work, I don't know when I'd be able to get there.  Maybe I'll give them a jingle anyway.... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>George I. Miller<BR>Fiero Shop, Richmond, Ca.<BR>Toll free: <B>866-534-8486</B><BR>(510) 23-FIERO<BR>(510) 233-4376<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||RiceCooker||04-12-2001||06:01 PM||||Thanks for the help<P>I'm not thinkin there's any reason why i would get shafted either. That's why i was checkin if anyone else has experienced difficulties. I talked to George on the phone several times and he seemed honest. It wasnt picked up Monday or Tuesday. Yesterday (Wednesday) he said, "this afternoon" and today it was still there.<P>Just my frustrations are adding up, that's all. But I won't take it out on all of you.<P>I LOVE MY PFF FAMILY  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Kids in the back seat cause accidents<BR>Accidents in the back seat cause kids||||reg||6
Z||000004||c m west||04-12-2001||06:33 PM||||Believe me, I have no problem selling parts to people all over the world - but in ALL Honesty, shipping to Canada is an absolute ***** , mainly because UPS does not recognize the NAFTA treaty, and dealings with the W.T.O. - after going through customs, service charges, and way bills - a $20 part can EASILY climb to $100<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phaeton||04-13-2001||02:40 AM||||UPS and international borders do not seem to get along well.<P>Multipackage shipments sent second day air from the same company on the same day have taken three to five days to arrive, especially frustrating when the box with the packing slip arrives on day five.<P>I would have thought the packages would travel together or at least in the same time period, but they don't.<P>The physical reality is that crossing an international border can add one to three days travel time without any pattern or logical reason.<P>I have dealt with the Fieroshop and they are straight talking folk there.<P>PS--Unless the company is on a scheduled UPS stop packages get picked up the day following notification.||||reg||12
Z||000006||thomas_l||04-13-2001||08:56 AM||||It's a pain because everything must go through a customs agent. I've had good success with FedEx for US/Canada shipments. You need to make sure that you have a manifest (invoice) with reasonable values on the contents plus appropriate taxes. FedEx will give you the necessary forms and collect the import/export duties from the shipper. If all is in order, your shipment should sail through customs and not lose days (weeks!) due to the gov getting their part.||||reg||1
Z||000007||RiceCooker||04-13-2001||10:20 AM||||Good news is the part went out yesterday (Thursday) and it's on the way  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I have recently dealt with UPS and i was very pleased. It was for my Pearl Jam bootlegs from Sony Music in GA.||||reg||1
Z||000008||BAM-BAM||04-13-2001||10:28 AM||||I have had the same problem with UPS tracking. First off, it was probably shipped UPS ground, to Canada that could be a week or more from California. Second, the UPS tracking system dose not always get updated correctly. I had parts sent from the Fiero Store (i believe) and tried to track them and never once were they updated and they arrived on time. Anyhoogles, relax bro, I'm sure that George and Terry aren't going to screw you.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Peace, B2, OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||RiceCooker||04-13-2001||10:35 AM||||No, it's all cool. I was just getting a little anxious.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||SteveJ||04-13-2001||10:49 AM||||I ship computer monitors back to the gateway factory for warantee replacement. UPS guy just looks at it every day for a week or more before taking it. ( He says the truck is full. )||||reg||1
Z||000011||TheFiero64||04-13-2001||05:37 PM||||I see it was picked up. If it is a schedule pickup, The driver will pick up every day. If not, they will have to call for a 1 time pickup. It may take a day for this to go through. If a package is to be sent out by air, then you can call for an on the spot "On Call Air". The driver will get a message showing the address to pick up the package and asks for his ETA for picking it up. He can not bypass this screen and must respond. If a pickup is missed, the driver will get in big trouble!  <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000012||TheFiero64||04-13-2001||05:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Phaeton:<BR><B>UPS and international borders do not seem to get along well.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't think they have any border trouble. I know we are the biggest international shipper in the business. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>UPS Daily International Flights 142<P><B>UPS INTERNATIONAL</B><P>[list] <BR><LI>UPS serves more than 200 countries and territories worldwide using more than 570 aircraft. <BR><LI>UPS has spent $11 billion on technology in the last 15 years - more than it spent on trucks. <BR><LI>ups.com is accessible in 15 languages and dialects, and has dedicated content for 112 countries.<BR><LI>UPS Customhouse Brokerage is one of the world's largest brokerages with more than 3000 employees and 77 dedicated offices in 34 countries.<P><B>EUROPE</B><BR><LI>UPS delivers by 8:30 a.m. to more business centers in Europe than <B>anyone in the industry</B> - part of the company's unsurpassed regional portfolio of time-definite, guaranteed services.<BR><LI>UPS laid the groundwork for a borderless Europe by introducing a first-to-market uniform portfolio of express services, documentation and billing across the region. <P><B>ASIA PACIFIC</B><P><LI>In China, UPS has branded operations in 21 key cities and delivers to 108 cities through its joint venture with Sinotrans.<BR> <BR><LI>UPS has invested $400 million in its Asia Pacific air network and $22 million in its new regional headquarters in Singapore (scheduled for completion in 2001). <BR>LATIN AMERICA & THE CARIBBEAN<P><BR><LI>UPS offers more guaranteed services to and from the United States than any other carrier in the region.<BR> <BR><LI>The acquisition of Challenge Air Cargo will make UPS the largest air cargo and express carrier in the region and more than double the number of airports UPS serves. <P><B>CANADA</B><P><BR><LI>UPS is the only courier to offer guaranteed delivery by 8 a.m. the next business day to major cities in Canada and offers the broadest portfolio of guaranteed, time-definite delivery options in the industry. <P><LI>UPS Canada can provide customs clearance for all cross-border shipments, regardless of carrier or mode of transportation by land, sea or air. <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
Z||000013||TheFiero64||04-13-2001||05:51 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SteveJ:<BR><B>I ship computer monitors back to the gateway factory for warantee replacement. UPS guy just looks at it every day for a week or more before taking it. ( He says the truck is full. )</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I would call UPS and file a driver complaint. He should not do that. If he is that full with pickups then he should be getting some releif from another driver. It is guys like that that give us a bad rap.<P><p>[This message has been edited by TheFiero64 (edited 04-13-2001).]||||reg||1
